# ~
#
# Build context exclusions for orbit
#
# Both images build with the repository root as context, so everything here
# would otherwise be sent to the daemon and be available to a COPY. The first
# two blocks are about size and cache churn; the third is about secrets.
#
# ------------------------------------------------


# version control and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.github

# environments and caches -- .venv in particular is hundreds of megabytes of
# host-built wheels that would be wrong inside the image even if copied
.venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache

# tests and documentation. neither is installed into the image, and both
# change often enough to invalidate the context for no gain
apps/*/tests
docs
*.md

# secrets. apps/gate/.env holds the auth0 client secret and the tenant's
# details. it is gitignored, so it is not in a clone -- but it *is* in a
# working tree, and a build context is not a clone. the container receives
# these values at run time through compose's env_file, never baked into a
# layer where anyone with the image can read them back.
.env
*.env
env/
